Gas-n-Go is a chain of auto body shops in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]. Its shop at 412 Anchor Boulevard in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] is a small one-story building on a busy street of through traffic: gas pumps under an awning out front, a garage of three bays to one side, a counter and a store level inside, and alleys with dumpsters and a service door down the left side.

Under the shop, past a locked back door on the store level, is a [[Hearts|Heart]]'s fane, and none of it matches the shop above. A spiral stair turns counterclockwise between stained glass showing one continuous fire, the air is warm, and the floor and inner wall are dull steel plating with pneumatics moving beneath them, like the building breathing. The stair is narrow enough for one person at a time. At its foot, a steel-and-glass hall leads to a glass bridge over a gap, with a throne on a raised altar at the far end.

The [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] hid [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] in that fane. The Party's own car sat in one of the shop's bays on a hoist while the gang worked on it, and the Party found its keys on a rack by the counter before going down the stair.
